<resources>
    <!--
      WL-409: phones are locked to portrait, tablets are not.

      Wireframe §19 makes portrait the primary target and sets a hard rule for
      the game screen: "the input and Submit button should not be hidden below
      the keyboard". On a phone in landscape they already are — the
      required-letter callout fills the short axis on its own, the input lands
      on the bottom edge before the keyboard even opens, and Submit and Hint
      sit below the fold. Redesigning the core screen for a viewport it was
      never drawn for is not v1 work, so the orientation is locked and the
      decision is recorded (Delivery Plan, WL-409).

      `screenOrientation` is an enum attribute, so this is an *integer*
      resource, not a string: the values are `ActivityInfo`'s own constants.
      1 = SCREEN_ORIENTATION_PORTRAIT. A string resource here resolves to
      nothing and the activity silently falls back to unspecified — which is
      exactly what happened on the first attempt at this, and it rotated.

      Tablets override this in values-sw600dp. iOS already ships the same
      split: portrait-only on iPhone, all four orientations on iPad
      (Info.plist's UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~ipad).
    -->
    <integer name="screen_orientation">1</integer>
</resources>
